  },
  {
   "date": "1986-08-03",
   "kind": "construction",
   "description": "Work to turn the convent of Most Holy Redeemer Church into Coming Home Hospice, a residential hospice for people with AIDS and other terminal illnesses, began at 115 Diamond Street with a ceremony on Sunday 3 August 1986. The paper put the cost at $450,000.",
   "source": "bay-area-reporter-BAR_19860731-n20"
  },
  {
   "date": "1987-02-19",
   "kind": "opening",
   "description": "Coming Home Hospice opened with 15 beds, ten of them reserved for people dying of AIDS, and was to take its first patients on 2 March 1987. The paper put the money raised for the conversion at $704,000, nearly half of it from the gay and lesbian community.",
